// ★ `@diverges` — the one exception to "everything terminates", and why it is an ATTRIBUTE.
//
// The first attempt used the effect row (`effects diverge`), and the corpus refused it: the row
// is a COMPLETE upper bound, so declaring one bit obliges you to declare them all — a `main`
// that also prints got [E130] for an incomplete row. Opting out of termination would have meant
// spelling out every other effect, which is the verbosity the inference exists to avoid.
//
// Divergence is one rare property of one declaration. That is exactly what `@cold`, `@hot` and
// `@noreturn` already are, so it joins them and leaves the row alone.
extern proc libc_printf(fmt *u8, ...) i32
proc serve(n i32) i32 effects diverge, io {
    var i i32 = 0
    while i < n { }
    return libc_printf("%d\n", i)
}
proc main() i32 { return 0 }
